target/

# Cargo.lock was ignored here because this crate path-depends on its sibling:
# a committed lockfile went stale on every nucl-parquet release and tripped the
# pre-commit hook. The workspace removes that failure mode — there is now one
# lockfile at clients/rs/Cargo.lock covering both crates, so it moves with them
# instead of lagging one behind. It is tracked, which is what a published binary
# wants for reproducible builds.
